# Recorded verification baselines for scripts/verify.sh
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Every agent and every human composed verification ad-hoc, so every one had
# different gaps. The numbers below are the recorded truth of what a green
# tree produces. `scripts/verify.sh` compares against them rather than against
# whatever the runner happens to remember, so "it passed" means the same thing
# to everyone.
#
# HOW EACH NUMBER IS COMPARED
# ---------------------------
# Test counts are FLOORS. Adding tests never fails the gate; losing them does.
# That is the direction that matters: the failure this repo actually suffered
# was a suite silently shrinking (a fail-fast run reporting 124 of 488 suites
# as a complete pass), not a suite growing.
#
# Clippy warnings are a CEILING. New lint debt fails; paying debt down does not.
#
# WHEN THE ACTUAL EXCEEDS A FLOOR, verify.sh still passes but prints a STALE
# notice naming the new number. Updating this file is then a deliberate,
# reviewable one-line commit — never a silent drift.
#
# HOW TO RE-MEASURE
# -----------------
#   scripts/verify.sh --full --show-actuals
# prints every measured number in this file's format. Copy the ones you intend
# to move. Do not lower a floor to make a red tree green: a floor that dropped
# means tests were deleted, which is the finding, not the fix.

# `cargo test --locked --lib -j2` from the repo root.
# The root crate's in-`src/` unit tests only.
BASELINE_ROOT_LIB_TESTS=1228

# `cargo test --locked --no-fail-fast -j2` from the repo root, total `passed`
# summed across every `test result:` line.
BASELINE_ROOT_FULL_TESTS=5353

# Number of test binaries the full sweep actually RUNS (counted from cargo's
# own `Running ...` lines). This is the specific guard against the fail-fast
# trap: a run that executes a fraction of the suites and still reports a clean
# summary is caught here even if every executed suite passed.
BASELINE_ROOT_TEST_BINARIES=491

# `cargo test --locked -j2` inside apps/desktop/src-tauri.
# NOTE: plain `cargo test`, never `--lib` — that crate is bin-only and has no
# lib target, so `cargo test --lib` fails there outright.
BASELINE_DESKTOP_TESTS=282

# `npm test` inside apps/desktop — the `<n>/<total> test files passed.` count.
# A zero here is treated as a hard failure regardless of the floor: the runner
# reports 0/0 as success when node_modules is missing, which is the exact
# false-green verify.sh exists to prevent.
BASELINE_FRONTEND_TEST_FILES=85

# `cargo clippy --locked --tests -j2`, counting real diagnostic warnings —
# cargo's own per-target "generated N warnings" summary lines are excluded so a
# warning is never counted twice.
#
# Split per crate because they are separate cargo invocations: a root-only
# clippy run never lints apps/desktop/src-tauri, which is the same blind spot
# that let that crate ship un-compilable twice.
#
# MEASURED 2026-07-30 on a clean tranche/6 tree, fresh target dir, exit 0 both.
# The "80" and "83" figures circulating in docs/release/v0.6/ could not be
# reproduced by any counting method against this command; docs/architecture/
# testing.md contradicts them again by documenting `-- -D warnings`, which
# cannot be passing at any non-zero baseline. All three are stale. These two
# numbers are what the command actually produces.
BASELINE_CLIPPY_WARNINGS_ROOT=76
BASELINE_CLIPPY_WARNINGS_DESKTOP=7

# `cargo run --locked --bin v06_class_state_dump` — every class must compute at
# every level, i.e. `levels_blocked: []` for all of them.
BASELINE_COMPUTED_CLASSES=27
